From: Ze kernel maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] ppp: bind channel operations to held original files

Apply after the original-file link/address, route and family/alias guards.
The caller must supply genuine original /dev/ppp channel files through the
following atomic PPPoX capture patch; an os.File wrapper alone does not prove
original channel ownership.

Add versioned fixed-layout CONNECT/DISCONNECT and BRIDGE/UNBRIDGE peer-file
forms plus a non-mutating bound-channel capability query. The unit form
requires the actual original creator struct file, including true duplicates.
An attached non-owner unit file cannot authorize live or retired cleanup.
Resolve no unit/channel number in the new commands. Compare original
namespace pairs and actual relationship pointers before native effects.

Keep ppp->owner as non-owning creator provenance after external unregister;
release unregisters only a live registered device. A bound file cannot rebind
private_data, and the retired unit has no IDR entry for new file attachment.
The pointer is compared, never dereferenced or retained as a self-reference.
This permits genuine cleanup after unit-number reuse without an extra birth
field, while the existing live owner probe still refuses a retired device.

Close channel admission under upl before unregister's first detach. Serialize
the shared native relationship producers through the existing chan_sem and
retain it through list/refcount/grace-period settlement. Pair operations use
one mutex/upl address order. An already absent expected relationship succeeds
only after prior native operation settlement. Guarded bridge creation checks
both live channels before publishing either direction; cleanup changes only
the actual expected relationship and preserves an unrelated peer.

Take fget before RTNL, then use RTNL + ppp_mutex trylock to avoid the existing
ppp_mutex-to-RTNL inversion. Drop the file after both locks. No file descriptor
is closed, duplicated or retained by the borrowed operation. Current legacy
entry points remain; product callers must require the positive feature receipt
and use the new forms, with no fallback on ENOTTY or a missing bit.

